From 42fed98edc0926e6e8aa2423b3435be982dbd06e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: STX Hardening <noreply@example.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 00:04:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix client panel access: own path, role-aware login redirect

Root cause: the client panel (customers' server list) lives at '/', the same URL as the storefront, so
signed-in customers could never reach it and Filament's post-login redirect (Filament::getUrl() = '/')
dropped everyone on the storefront. The storefront also redirected signed-in users to /customer-orders,
so the real server list was unreachable.

- Client panel moves to its own path (APP_CLIENT_PATH, default /app): /app, /app/login, /app/customer-orders
- LoginResponse::homeUrl(): admins -> /admin, everyone else -> client panel; intended URL still honoured
- RedirectToAdmin now defaults to on (admins can switch it off in their profile)
- RedirectIfAuthenticated and OAuth login use the same role-aware home
- Storefront no longer hijacks signed-in visitors, so customers can browse and order more servers
- routes/auth.php: /login redirected to /login (a loop once the panel moves); now forwards to the panel login
- Legacy /customer-orders and /account forward to the new addresses
- Fix links: storefront header/footer, help center ('/servers' never existed), Pelican footer
- compose/.env.example/README/staging checklist updated
